texts.text:
1. objectively report the action of the story;
2. go into the mind of any character;
3. interpret for us that character’s appearance, speech, 
actions, and thoughts, even if the character cannot do so;
4. move freely in time or space to give us a panoramic, 
telescopic, microscopic, or historical view, telling us what 
has happened elsewhere or in the past or what will happen 
in the future; and
5. provide general reflections, judgments, and truths.
